note ── The answer ──
note The system is not going to fix itself and it is not your job to fix it.
note The move is to route AROUND it.
note
note FIVE CONCRETE MOVES:
note
note 1. DIRECT MONETIZATION — Patreon Substack paid community
note    The people who already watch you will pay you directly.
note    No algorithm. No brand approval. No diversity budget ceiling.
note    Even 500 people at $10/month is $5000/month.
note
note 2. BRAND TARGETING — not diversity budgets
note    Target brands with a documented racial equity commitment
note    (Ben and Jerrys Patagonia Brand Neutral Black-owned brands)
note    These brands have main budget for this not a silo.
note    Also target mental health ADHD autism advocacy brands who need
note    an authentic neurodivergent voice they cannot manufacture.
note
note 3. COLLECTIVE LEVERAGE
note    The Creator Ink network and Black creator collectives negotiate
note    rates collectively. One creator pitching alone gets a low offer.
note    Ten creators pitching together get a different conversation.
note
note 4. MAKE THE DISPARITY THE CONTENT
note    The gap itself is the story. Documenting what you earn vs what
note    white creators earn for the same work attracts the exact audience
note    that feels this same thing. That audience is large and loyal
note    and they will pay you directly for naming what they already know.
note
note 5. GRANTS AND ARTS FUNDING
note    Sundance Institute Black Creator programs
note    Black Girl Ventures
note    NAACP Accelerator
note    SXSW Creator Fund
note    These are not brand deals. They do not come with brand approval.
note    They pay for exactly the voice that brands call risky.
